  "comment": "Maps schedule ids to media files, paths relative to the repo root. Since 2026-09-29 the main-task stimuli are still PICTURES, not video clips: the id is the file stem in stimuli/images/ (animals_1 is stimuli/images/animals_1.png), made from the originals stimuli/<category>_<n>.png by stimuli/make_clean_images.py. Four everyday categories of three exemplars for the 4-step task, and since 2026-10-05 the space set for the 3-step task: aliens, spaceships, planets, in this fixed order (originals in stimuli/alien_images/). The ids are fixed for all participants: per-participant randomization (category order per step, exemplar per journey) lives in the schedule's A1..C4 columns. Reward images since 2026-10-06: money, a gold relic and a diamond (stimuli/rewards/treasure_*.png, built by stimuli/make_reward_images.py from reward4, reward2 and reward1); the earlier placeholders money.png, gold.png, diamonds.png are kept. Since 2026-10-23 the space set and the treasures are the FINAL stimuli (stimuli/final/, built by stimuli/make_final_stimuli.py from final_stimuli/favorites/): stills on mid-grey for every session and every screen, and for the MRI the 24 frames of each 1 s video ('frames', 'reward_frames'), played in the walks and on the outcome screen; the earlier white-card pictures stay in stimuli/images/ and stimuli/rewards/. Since 2026-10-26 also 'video' and 'reward_videos': the same frames as H.264 for the browser, which plays them online.",
